Internal review threshold: £1,500 (fictional)
Normal: £200–£900, 1–2 transfers/month, near payday,
        higher at Dashain/Tihar
Suspicious share: ~4% of customers

Typologies:
1. Structuring: repeated transfers £1,300–£1,499 in a short window
2. Rapid in-and-out: funds received and sent within hours
3. Many-to-one: many unrelated senders to one beneficiary
4. Velocity spike: normally ~£300 monthly, suddenly 15 transfers in a week
5. Dormant then active: long inactivity then sudden bursts
6. Mule-style: third-party funded, high turnover, fast pass-through
7. Unexplained relationship / profile mismatch
8. Volume exceeds declared profile (4x+ expected monthly volume)
